1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,130
If you pressed these pads

2
00:00:01,130 --> 00:00:02,390
against a glass wall,

3
00:00:02,390 --> 00:00:03,370
you could lift your feet

4
00:00:03,370 --> 00:00:04,060
off the ground—

5
00:00:04,060 --> 00:00:05,980
and climb it like Spider-Man.

6
00:00:05,980 --> 00:00:07,190
Their surfaces are covered

7
00:00:07,190 --> 00:00:08,990
in microscopic wedges.

8
00:00:08,990 --> 00:00:10,230
As you pull downward,

9
00:00:10,230 --> 00:00:11,420
the wedges bend flat

10
00:00:11,420 --> 00:00:12,730
against the glass.

11
00:00:12,730 --> 00:00:14,090
This brings them so close

12
00:00:14,090 --> 00:00:15,850
that tiny molecular attractions

13
00:00:15,850 --> 00:00:17,780
can hold your entire weight.

14
00:00:17,780 --> 00:00:19,760
Special springs spread the load,

15
00:00:19,760 --> 00:00:20,830
so one little patch

16
00:00:20,830 --> 00:00:22,650
doesn’t have to hold you up alone.

17
00:00:22,650 --> 00:00:24,140
Then, you shift your weight

18
00:00:24,140 --> 00:00:25,590
onto the other pad.

19
00:00:25,590 --> 00:00:26,710
The first releases,

20
00:00:26,710 --> 00:00:27,340
letting you reach

21
00:00:27,340 --> 00:00:28,920
higher and repeat.

22
00:00:28,920 --> 00:00:30,130
But there’s a catch.

23
00:00:30,130 --> 00:00:31,500
They need a smooth surface

24
00:00:31,500 --> 00:00:32,340
to grip.

25
00:00:32,340 --> 00:00:33,910
So you can climb glass—

26
00:00:33,910 --> 00:00:35,440
but switch to rough brick,

27
00:00:35,440 --> 00:00:36,870
and those microscopic wedges

28
00:00:36,870 --> 00:00:38,670
can’t make the same contact.

